    "title": "Proxy, in one breath",
    "items": [
     "Eagerly creating expensive objects wasted time and memory on things no one ever used.",
     "The client only needs the interface \u2014 so a lightweight stand-in can implement it and defer the real work.",
     "Proxy: same interface as the real object, holds it, and controls access \u2014 here, creating it lazily on first use."
    ],
    "challenge": "You call a slow remote pricing service. You want callers to use it like a local object, but cache each result for 60 seconds.",
    "question": "Does Proxy fit? What's the subject, the real subject, and what does this proxy control?",
    "dur": 52.831
   }
